      "The image is comic: a person walking around with a log protruding from one eye, trying to perform delicate eye surgery on a brother who has a speck. The picture would be funny if it were not so common. Jesus's prescription is sharp: first deal with the log. Self-examination is the prerequisite for godly correction of others. The believer who never examines themselves has nothing to offer. The believer who has spent serious time with their own log can, at the right moment, gently and honestly help with someone else's speck.",
