      "Jesus reinforces with a domestic image. What father, if his son asks for bread, gives him a stone? Or a fish, gives him a serpent? Even broken human fathers know to give good gifts. How much more will the Father in heaven give good things — Luke's version says specifically 'the Holy Spirit' — to those who ask Him. The Father is not reluctant. He is not tired of you. He is not running low. Ask.",
